From: AX6 NSS Repair Project
Date: Sun, 3 Aug 2026 11:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] mailbox: qcom-apcs-ipc: bound max_register by actual resource size

The global apcs_regmap_config.max_register is hard-coded to 0x1008 to
accommodate SDX55 (offset=0x1008), but this value exceeds the MMIO
resource size on IPQ8074/IPQ6018 (0x1000 bytes).  When userspace reads
the regmap debugfs `registers` node, the regmap core iterates from 0 to
max_register inclusive with stride 4, accessing offset 0x1008 which lies
beyond the mapped region:

  Unable to handle kernel paging request at virtual address ffffffc080e86000
  ESR = 0x0000000096000007  (DABT, current EL)
  FSC = 0x07: level 3 translation fault
  pc : regmap_mmio_read32le+0x8/0x20
  Call trace:
   regmap_mmio_read32le
   _regmap_bus_reg_read
   _regmap_read
   regmap_read
   regmap_read_debugfs
   regmap_map_read_file
   full_proxy_read  →  vfs_read  →  ksys_read
   ... el0_svc ...
  Kernel panic - not syncing: Oops: Fatal exception

Fix by computing the safe max_register at probe time from the actual
resource size.  A local copy of apcs_regmap_config is used so that
SDX55 (whose resource covers the full 0x1008) is not affected.

The clock child device (when present) accesses register offset 8 or 16,
both well within the bounded range on all SoCs.

Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Signed-off-by: AX6 NSS Repair Project
---
 drivers/mailbox/qcom-apcs-ipc-mailbox.c | 14 +++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/mailbox/qcom-apcs-ipc-mailbox.c
+++ b/drivers/mailbox/qcom-apcs-ipc-mailbox.c
@@ -70,18 +70,31 @@ static int qcom_apcs_ipc_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	struct qcom_apcs_ipc *apcs;
 	const struct qcom_apcs_ipc_data *apcs_data;
 	struct regmap *regmap;
+	struct regmap_config regmap_config_local;
+	struct resource *res;
 	void __iomem *base;
 	unsigned long i;
 	int ret;
 
 	apcs = devm_kzalloc(&pdev->dev, sizeof(*apcs), GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (!apcs)
 		return -ENOMEM;
 
+	res = platform_get_resource(pdev, IORESOURCE_MEM, 0);
+	if (!res)
+		return -ENODEV;
+
 	base = devm_platform_ioremap_resource(pdev, 0);
 	if (IS_ERR(base))
 		return PTR_ERR(base);
 
-	regmap = devm_regmap_init_mmio(&pdev->dev, base, &apcs_regmap_config);
+	/*
+	 * Bound max_register to the actual resource size so that
+	 * debugfs regmap reads cannot access beyond the mapped region.
+	 */
+	regmap_config_local = apcs_regmap_config;
+	regmap_config_local.max_register = resource_size(res) -
+					   apcs_regmap_config.reg_stride;
+	regmap = devm_regmap_init_mmio(&pdev->dev, base, &regmap_config_local);
 	if (IS_ERR(regmap))
 		return PTR_ERR(regmap);
